=== Text #5 ===
> [Sugar] And Our Kids: Are We Doing Enough?
[When] my son eats a major[ sugar] bomb, like a piece of cake at a birthday party, I can see his mood change. His generally sweet and cooperative disposition shifts to one of a fired up wild child, which is soon followed by a crash of energy and[ crank]iness. His ability[ to] follow directions, typically a positive trait[ for] my son, wanes as a result as well.
Watching this outwardly behavioral[ roller] coaster is like tracing the steps of[ sugar]’s overt and undeniable physiological impact[ on] my son. The sugar is sending signals and triggering reactions in his young and developing mind and body.[]

