> ["]Dozens of network-att[ached] storage (NAS) servers and other consumer appliances are about to gain[ mainline] kernel and Debian GNU/Linux support. The 2.6.25 kernel, currently in the final stages of testing, will support Mar[vell]'s F[ero]ceon micro-[arch]itecture and 'Orion' SoCs, with Debian support close behind, sources say.
